course: dictionary
lesson: 14837
title: The word radiograph
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A radiograph is a picture made with X-rays. X-rays can pass through soft parts of the body, but they show bones and teeth more clearly. «The doctor looked at the radiograph of my arm and saw a crack in the bone.» The doctor is looking at a picture, not at the arm itself.
explain: Radiograph is the formal, medical word. In everyday talk, people usually say «X-ray». «The dentist took a dental radiograph of my teeth» means the dentist took an X-ray picture of the teeth. The word dental tells you which part of the body the picture is of.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. Words like doctor, bone, teeth or chest tell you a radiograph is being used to look inside the body. You can check your meaning by swapping in «X-ray»: if the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: A radiograph is an X-ray picture of the inside of the body or an object.
fact: «Radiograph» is the formal or medical word; most people say «X-ray».
fact: A person who takes radiographs is called a radiographer.
fact: «Chest radiograph» means an X-ray picture of the chest, and «dental radiograph» means an X-ray picture of the teeth.
fact: You can use the word «X-ray» instead of radiograph in everyday talk, but a doctor or scientist may say radiograph.
exercise: «The doctor looked at the radiograph and saw a crack in the bone.» What is a radiograph? | A kind of bone | *An X-ray picture of the inside of the body | A doctor's bag | A long, thin needle
exercise: «A radiographer took a chest radiograph to check my lungs.» Who takes radiographs? | *A radiographer | A gardener | A lollipop lady | A baker
exercise: In everyday speech, which word means the same as radiograph? | Map | Sunshine | *X-ray | Telephone
test: «The dentist took a dental radiograph of my teeth.» What does dental radiograph mean? | *An X-ray picture of the teeth | A picture of the ears | A dentist's chair | A picture of the sky
test: Mia says, «The chest radiograph showed my lungs were healthy.» Which part of the body was in the picture? | The head | The legs | The feet | *The chest
exam: Lily says, «The radiograph shows the bones in my hand.» What does radiograph mean? | A doctor's visit | A bone in the hand | *An X-ray picture of the inside of the body | A kind of hand cream
